Hmmm. If I specify the name of a previously saved character (or I'm on
a multi-user system where I'm forced to use my id as my character
name), I think all it'll allow me to do is to load the saved game and
continue with it.  This means that for any given 'standard id', there
can only be two games - the highest scoring one in the log file and
the one currently in play.  One the one in play is over, it'll either
replace the high scoring one or be lost.

Now, if you want to mess around behind its back, copying save files in
and out of the save dirctory, then all bets are off, but if you play
within what NetHack allows, then it's not a big problem.

